{"id":908,"date":"2025-08-11T20:30:24","date_gmt":"2025-08-11T18:30:24","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/sunsets-in-menorca\/"},"modified":"2026-07-02T13:52:51","modified_gmt":"2026-07-02T11:52:51","slug":"sunset-menorca-9-viewpoints","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/sunset-menorca-9-viewpoints\/","title":{"rendered":"Sunsets in Menorca"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Menorca has sunsets that stick in your memory. Beyond the famous beaches, there are discreet viewpoints, lighthouses and cliffs where the sky lights up with oranges and violets. I&#8217;m <strong>Daniel Vaquera<\/strong>, official local guide for Voyager Menorca, and here are my 9 favorite places \u2014with practical tips, recommended wind and little tricks\u2014 so you can enjoy the sunset like a Menorcan.  <\/p>\n<nav aria-label=\"Contenido\">\n<strong>Content<\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"#cuando-como\">When and how to best enjoy it<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#pont-den-gil\">Pont d&#8217;en Gil<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#punta-nati\">Punta Nati Lighthouse<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#cala-morell\">Cala Morell Viewpoints<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#cala-en-brut\">Cala en Brut<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#artrutx\">Artrutx Lighthouse<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#cavalleria\">Cavalleria Lighthouse<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#sanitja\">Port de Sanitja<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#xoroi\">Cova d&#8217;en Xoroi<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#monte-toro\">Monte Toro<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"#que-llevar\">What to bring<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"#amaneceres\">Bonus: sunrises<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"#faq\">FAQ<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/nav>\n<section id=\"cuando-como\">\n<h2>When and how to best enjoy it<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Arrive 40\u201350 minutes early.<\/strong> The good colors start before the sun touches the horizon and explode 10\u201315 minutes after sunset.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Watch the wind.<\/strong> If <strong>tramontana (N)<\/strong> is blowing, the north is clearer; with <strong>migjorn (S)<\/strong>, the south coast feels friendlier.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Safety and respect.<\/strong> Closed shoes, flashlight for the return, and always away from the edge of the cliff. Leave no trace: Menorca is a <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/menorca-biosphere-reserve\/\">Biosphere Reserve<\/a>. <\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"pont-den-gil\">\n<h2>1) Pont d&#8217;en Gil (Ciutadella)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> a perfect natural arch to see how the sun &#8220;hides&#8221; behind the rock.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> park near Cam\u00ed de sa Farola and follow the path (10\u201315 min).<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> stay 10 minutes after sunset; the sky turns magenta and the arch silhouettes the scene like a painting.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"punta-nati\">\n<h2>2) Punta Nati Lighthouse (Ciutadella)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> lunar landscape, silence and a clear horizon to the northwest. The lighthouse was built in 1913 after the shipwreck of the <em>G\u00e9n\u00e9ral Chanzy<\/em>; you can find the full story in the <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/guia-faros-menorca\/\">lighthouse guide<\/a>. <\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> narrow road; arrive early to park in the designated area.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> take a jacket even in summer; the wind here is deceiving.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"cala-morell\">\n<h2>3) Cala Morell Viewpoints (Ciutadella)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> dramatic cliffs and white houses that are tinged with gold.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> several natural terraces signposted above the development.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> lean out (with caution) to the north end; there are usually fewer people and the angle is beautiful.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"cala-en-brut\">\n<h2>4) Cala en Brut (Ciutadella)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> rock platforms over an intense blue fjord.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> easy from the development; ideal if you want to take a last evening swim.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> find a low platform for reflections of &#8220;liquid gold&#8221; in the water.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"artrutx\">\n<h2>5) Artrutx Lighthouse (Cap d&#8217;Artrutx \u2013 Ciutadella)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> iconic lighthouse with the sun setting to the southwest and views of Mallorca on clear days.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> fully paved road; nearby cafeteria.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> ideal for families or if you want a &#8220;comfortable&#8221; sunset with a chair and a drink. This is the option we recommend in <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/menorca-con-ninos-en-un-dia-ciutadella\/\">Menorca with children<\/a>. <\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"cavalleria\">\n<h2>6) Cavalleria Lighthouse (Es Mercadal)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> the highest cliff in the north and a 180\u00b0 panoramic view.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> road to the lighthouse; respect designated parking areas.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> explore (staying on the paths) towards the west side to find quieter spots. Combine it with a prior swim at <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/las-mejores-playas-de-menorca-y-cuales-evitar-en-temporada-alta\/\">Cavalleria beach<\/a>. <\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"sanitja\">\n<h2>7) Port de Sanitja (Es Mercadal)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> an ancient natural harbor \u2014with a Roman past\u2014 and mirror-like sunsets.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> next to Cavalleria; easy paths.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> bring a tripod if you like photography: perfect reflections when the water is calm.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"xoroi\">\n<h2>8) Cova d&#8217;en Xoroi (Cala en Porter \u2013 Alaior)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> the sun sinks in front of a cave hanging from the cliff: a very theatrical experience.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> paid entrance and limited capacity; it&#8217;s advisable to arrive with plenty of time.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> book the sunset pass and look for side balconies to avoid crowds.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"monte-toro\">\n<h2>9) Monte Toro (Es Mercadal)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why go:<\/strong> 358 m high \u2014the island&#8217;s rooftop, with the sanctuary of the Virgen del Toro\u2014 to see how all of Menorca changes color, with 360\u00b0 views.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Access:<\/strong> road to the summit; parking next to the sanctuary.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Local tip:<\/strong> if there&#8217;s airborne dust (calima), the sun turns intense red. Perfect for a telephoto lens. <\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"que-llevar\">\n<h2>What to bring (quick list)<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Water<\/strong>, something to snack on and a <strong>flashlight<\/strong> for the return.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Light jacket<\/strong>: even in August it cools down with the breeze.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Closed shoes<\/strong> if you are going to cliffs.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Trash bag<\/strong>: what you bring, you take with you.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"amaneceres\">\n<h2>Bonus: sunrises in the east<\/h2>\n<p>If you&#8217;re an early riser, note <strong>Fav\u00e0ritx<\/strong>, <strong>Sa Mesquida<\/strong> or <strong>Es Grau<\/strong>: pastel skies and total silence. Sunrise in Menorca has a different kind of peace. In <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/menorca-en-septiembre\/\">September<\/a>, with the sun rising later, you don&#8217;t even have to get up so early.  <\/p>\n<\/section>\n<section id=\"faq\">\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions<\/h2>\n<details>\n<summary>What&#8217;s the best place to watch the sunset in Menorca?<\/summary>\n<p>It depends on the wind and your plan: Pont d&#8217;en Gil and Punta Nati for dramatic scenery, Artrutx for comfort with family, Cavalleria for northern panoramic views, and Monte Toro for 360\u00b0.<\/p>\n<\/details>\n<details>\n<summary>What time should I arrive?<\/summary>\n<p>40\u201350 minutes in advance. The most intense colors arrive 10\u201315 minutes after the sun sets, so don&#8217;t leave right at dusk. <\/p>\n<\/details>\n<details>\n<summary>Is there an entrance fee at any viewpoint?<\/summary>\n<p>Only at Cova d&#8217;en Xoroi (ticketed entrance with limited capacity). The rest are free to access; please respect designated parking areas and paths. <\/p>\n<\/details>\n<\/section>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301?text=Hola%20Dani%2C%20nos%20gustar%C3%ADa%20una%20ruta%20de%20atardecer%20en%20Menorca.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>\ud83d\udcf2 Book a sunset tour via WhatsApp<\/strong><\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/field-trips\/\">See excursions<\/a><\/p>\n<h2>More Menorca guides<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/guia-faros-menorca\/\">Menorca\u2019s 7 lighthouses \u2192<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/las-mejores-playas-de-menorca-y-cuales-evitar-en-temporada-alta\/\">The best beaches in Menorca \u2192<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/discover-menorcas-secret-beaches-with-daniel-vaquera\/\">Beaches (almost) secret \u2192<\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/menorca-en-septiembre\/\">Menorca in September \u2192<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><script type=\"application\/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https:\/\/schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\n      \"mainEntityOfPage\": { \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"@id\": \"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/atardecer-menorca-9-miradores\/\" },\n      \"headline\": \"D\u00f3nde ver el atardecer en Menorca: 9 miradores con consejos de gu\u00eda local\",\n      \"description\":